diff --git a/Question-Type-Multiple-response.md b/Question-Type-Multiple-response.md
index d0ccd5e..22f7f2c 100644
--- a/Question-Type-Multiple-response.md
+++ b/Question-Type-Multiple-response.md
@@ -14,11 +14,11 @@ Questions with more than one right answer, e.g. "Which of these are irregular ve
 
 ## How it is scored
 
-Automatic. With partial credit on (the default), the score is the share of options the student got *right in either direction* — correctly ticked **and** correctly left blank. With it off, only an exact match scores.
+Automatic. With partial credit on (the default), each correct option ticked earns a share of the points (points ÷ number of correct options) and **each wrong option ticked cancels one share**; the score never goes below zero. A blank answer scores zero. With partial credit off, only an exact match scores.
 
 ## Watch out for
 
-- Because correctly *leaving out* a wrong option earns credit, a student who ticks nothing still scores on the options that were meant to stay empty. If that is not what you want, switch partial credit off.
+- Ticking everything scores zero, because each wrong tick cancels a correct one. This stops "select all" being a safe strategy. (Before 2026-11-19 the score also counted wrong options correctly left blank, so a blank answer earned most of the points.)
 
 ## Open research question
 
